# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Real financial data — never committed.
#
# legacy/ holds one household's actual balance history. Account numbers in the
# source were already masked, but the balances, the per-quarter net worth in the
# year notes, and the owner names are real. Git history is effectively permanent
# and this repository is intended to become public, so the data stays local.
#
# The *structural* artifacts below the ignores — the schema, the reconstructed
# queries, the extraction script — carry no personal data and are committed,
# because they document what the migration is migrating from.
#
# Regenerate everything here with: legacy/extracted/extract.sh
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
legacy/*.accdb
legacy/*.xlsx
legacy/extracted/csv/
legacy/extracted/*.sqlite
legacy/extracted/access-objects.csv
